.TH XD\-APPWIZ 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-appwiz \- Add or Remove Programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-appwiz
.RB [ \-\-add | \-\-components ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-appwiz
is Windows XP's Add or Remove Programs (Control Panel), through PackageKit
and Flatpak:
.TP
.B Change or Remove Programs
The programs in the Start menu, each with the package or Flatpak it came
from, its size, how often and when it was last used, and Remove.
.TP
.B Add New Programs
Install a package file, or search the software sources and Flatpak
remotes.
.TP
.B Add/Remove Windows Components
PackageKit's package groups.
.PP
Nothing runs as root: PackageKit and Flatpak's system helper ask polkit,
so
.BR xd\-polkit (1)
asks for an administrator's password when needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-add
Open on Add New Programs.
.TP
.B \-\-components
Open on Add/Remove Windows Components.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkcon (1),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR xd\-control (1)
